# text = Yea, they durst not make use of that which is their own lest they should offend their priests, who do yoke them according to their desires, and have brought them to believe, by their traditions and their dreams and their whims and their visions and their pretended mysteries, that they should, if they did not do according to their words, offend some unknown being, who they say is God-- a being who never has been seen or known, who never was nor ever will be.
# sent_id = 42
# llm_note = "Yea" = INTJ discourse on 'make'. "durst not make use of" = dare+neg+make+use (MWE: "make use of" = verb idiom, 'use' NOUN obj of make, 'of' case on 'that'). "that which is their own" = rel-clause nominal: 'that' PRON head, 'which' rel-pron nsubj of 'is', 'own' XCOMP of is. "lest" = SCONJ mark on 'offend' (purpose/fear clause). "who do yoke them" = acl:relcl on 'priests'; do=AUX (emphatic). "and have brought them to believe" = conj of 'yoke'. "by their traditions and..." = obl instrument of 'brought', with 5-way coord chain. "that they should...offend" = ccomp of 'believe'; contains parenthetical conditional "if they did not do according to their words". "who they say is God" = acl:relcl on 'being' (71); 'they say' = parenthetical ccomp; 'is God' main pred of rel-clause. "-- a being..." = appos on 'being'(71)/God, recharacterizing. Second 'being'(80): appos of God. "who never has been seen or known" = acl:relcl on second 'being'(80); seen+known coordinated VBN. "who never was nor ever will be" = second acl:relcl on being(80); 'nor' ADV advmod of 'was'; 'ever will be' = conj of 'was'.
